irement_affected"},"detail":"Typing (setFilter, Menu.qml:796) and opening another menu (setActiveMenu, Menu.qml:804, also reached from goBack) set pendingInitialMenu to empty, so a route summoned during startup never pulls the user out of what they chose, even if they went back to root. The rest of both functions, and the filter, navigation stack and back fallback these requirements state, are unchanged; their Implements lines now also name DK0D.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":796},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":804},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-DQ9P","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-DE93","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"info","title":"setFilter and setActiveMenu each gain one line that drops a waiting route (SW-REQ-260922-DQ9P, SW-REQ-260922-DE93)","verification":{"evidence":[{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-DE93","kind":"requirement"}],"method":"review.changes (spec, code-trace, function and call-level requirement impact)","note":"SW-REQ-260922-DE93 is in review.changes (code_changed, matchLevel file).","status":"confirmed"}},{"claim":{"params":{"requirement":"SW-REQ-260922-50RE"},"type":"requirement_affected"},"detail":"Menu.qml carries a file-level fingerprint, so any edit stales every requirement traced to it. All 29 were re-reviewed with citations: outside rebuildItemsFromSources, menuFilesAnswered, openExistingMenu, setFilter, setActiveMenu and the user FileView's onLoadFailed, every function is byte-identical and only shifted. Their clauses and FRETish are unchanged (review.changes: code_changed). 50RE (open/close/refresh dispatch) is named on the openExistingMenu and onLoadFailed Implements lines; its dispatch is unchanged.","refs":[{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-50RE","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-3JG5","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-3T3F","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-3VTN","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-4079","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-46HY","kin