ins/menu/Menu.qml:menuFilesAnswered","shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml:rebuildItemsFromSources"],"scenario":"in a live headless sway session, start quickshell with the user extension read delayed (and, separately, with the user extension absent), summon omarchy.menu with menu=system before the files load: the menu shows System once both files have answered, and an about override in the user file runs the user's command, not the default one"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"menuFilesAnswered reads defaultMenuFile.loaded and userMenuFile.loaded || userMenuFailed. The test and the harness model loaded as false until the first read lands, true from onLoaded on, false for a missing file, and true during a refresh() reload. The PR author reports checking this live on Quickshell 0.3.1 (a 20 MB file and a slow-open shim); this package does not drive a live shell. A missing DEFAULT file never sets loaded, so a route summoned then waits for the rest of the session (the menu shows root, as on quattro).","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":298},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":1060},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":1078},{"id":"SW-REQ-261002-DK0D","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Question: in a real Quickshell, does FileView.loaded behave as the gate assumes in every start-up case?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Live cold start with a delayed or missing user extension\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml:rebuildItemsFromSources"],"scenario":"summon a route during startup, press Down on root before the user file answers, then let it answer: the route opens and the cursor move is lost"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"Only typing (setFilter) and opening